WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.719 --> 00:00:05.430
Joel might be a gruff, grizzled survivor on
"The Last of Us," but Bella Ramsey says that

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:09.299
Pedro Pascal's on-set behavior is wildly different.

00:00:09.299 --> 00:00:14.210
Although it may seem like most video game-based
movies and television series seem to be destined

00:00:14.210 --> 00:00:18.140
for failure from the moment they're first
conceived, there's no question that HBO's

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:21.505
"The Last of Us" has found a cheat code to
buck that trend.

00:00:21.505 --> 00:00:26.480
And while there's plenty of possible reasons
for its success, many fans agree that Pedro

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:31.950
Pascal and Bella Ramsey's portrayals of tormented
survivor Joel and teenager Ellie are particularly

00:00:31.950 --> 00:00:32.925
bright spots.

00:00:32.925 --> 00:00:38.410
As with the original game, watching the unlikely
duo forge a close bond amid an anguish-filled,

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:43.230
post-apocalyptic world has served as the emotional
core of the series.

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:47.480
Pascal and Ramsey may have effective chemistry
as their characters in "The Last of Us," but

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:51.239
some viewers may be wondering about what their
real-world dynamic was like while they were

00:00:51.239 --> 00:00:52.544
filming on set.

00:00:52.544 --> 00:00:57.430
As it turns out, Ramsey has a lot to say about
Pascal's on-set behavior.

00:00:57.430 --> 00:01:01.221
During an interview with Screen Rant, Bella
Ramsey explained that working with Pedro Pascal

00:01:01.221 --> 00:01:04.620
was an incredibly fun experience from start
to finish.

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:09.504
She noted that what really stands out about
Pascal's personality is his overwhelming generosity.

00:01:09.504 --> 00:01:10.422
Ramsey said,

00:01:10.422 --> 00:01:12.199
"Working with Pedro was so fun.

00:01:12.199 --> 00:01:13.315
He's hilarious.

00:01:13.315 --> 00:01:15.600
He's probably one of the funniest people I've
ever met.

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:17.400
He's also incredibly generous.

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:19.877
That's the word that comes to mind when I
think of Pedro."

00:01:19.877 --> 00:01:20.749
She continued,

00:01:20.749 --> 00:01:24.035
"He's so generous with his words, with his
time, and with his actions.

00:01:24.035 --> 00:01:27.799
He's just a super cool person to be around,
and he definitely made the set a fun place

00:01:27.799 --> 00:01:28.510
to be."

00:01:28.510 --> 00:01:33.720
Ramsey went on to fondly recall the numerous
conversations she had with Pascal while filming.

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:37.280
As it happens, the pair were able to bond
over their shared "Game of Thrones" experience.

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:42.790
Ramsey played the young Lady of Bear Island,
Lyanna Mormont, while Pascal played the scene-stealing

00:01:42.790 --> 00:01:44.840
Oberyn Martell in the fantasy show.

00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:48.119
Though the two characters never shared the
screen, it seems like they still had plenty

00:01:48.119 --> 00:01:51.070
to talk about regarding their time on "Game
of Thrones."

00:01:51.070 --> 00:01:55.009
Specifically, Pascal has one object he'd love
to bring from the fantasy world of Westeros

00:01:55.009 --> 00:01:56.490
to "The Last of Us."

00:01:56.490 --> 00:01:58.270
"I really loved my robe."

00:01:58.643 --> 00:01:59.571
"I knew you were gonna say it.

00:01:59.571 --> 00:02:00.737
That's why I said clothing.

00:02:00.737 --> 00:02:02.772
I knew you were gonna say your robe."

00:02:02.772 --> 00:02:06.779
"Well, because it looked f–king awesome."

00:02:07.188 --> 00:02:12.220
As for filming their newest HBO show, it seems
that Pedro Pascal and Bella Ramsey relied

00:02:12.220 --> 00:02:13.830
on each other heavily.

00:02:13.830 --> 00:02:17.239
Pascal himself confirmed as much during an
interview with Entertainment Weekly, sharing

00:02:17.239 --> 00:02:21.730
that their mutual confusion and sense of unease
during the extensive shoot led them to become

00:02:21.730 --> 00:02:23.373
close friends in no time.

00:02:23.373 --> 00:02:27.660
"We never stopped being scared or [were] convinced
that we were getting it right, but at least

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:30.379
we could rely on each other without question."

00:02:30.379 --> 00:02:34.180
Pascal also mentions that his bond with Ramsey
came with a side effect, as their directors

00:02:34.180 --> 00:02:36.280
sometimes had trouble getting through to them.

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:37.070
He recalled,

00:02:37.070 --> 00:02:41.150
"There was so much time we got to spend together
on set that it was almost weird when we weren't

00:02:41.150 --> 00:02:43.440
together, as far as shooting was concerned.

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:45.300
There was this fascinating thing that would
happen.

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:47.739
We were just kind of in our own bubble no
matter what."

00:02:47.739 --> 00:02:51.800
"The Last of Us" may deal with some pretty
dark and depressing subject matter, but it

00:02:51.800 --> 00:02:56.519
seems that Pedro Pascal and Bella Ramsey actually
spent a lot of their shared time on set trying

00:02:56.519 --> 00:02:58.255
not to burst out laughing.

00:02:58.255 --> 00:03:02.906
When asked about one of his fondest memories
from set by Augustman, Pascal responded:

00:03:02.906 --> 00:03:04.819
"For me, it is those attacks of the giggles.

00:03:04.819 --> 00:03:08.830
I start to think about what I hear being suppressed
in Bella's throat, like a fungal disease the

00:03:08.830 --> 00:03:11.440
contagiousness of the laughter was brutal."

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:15.540
Ramsey echoed a similar answer, noting that
the duo were most prone to making each other

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:19.191
laugh while trying to film some of the most
gut-wrenching scenes in the show.

00:03:19.191 --> 00:03:21.760
As the actress recalled, they would laugh
even…

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:24.360
"...while talking about our characters' dead
family members.

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:27.278
It would start as a little giggle and then
would really grow."

00:03:27.278 --> 00:03:31.739
By all accounts, it seems that Pascal and
Ramsey got along swimmingly on set, and even

00:03:31.739 --> 00:03:36.085
helped lighten the emotional load on each
other when filming got particularly intense.

00:03:36.085 --> 00:03:40.310
That positive dynamic between the two lead
actors will hopefully continue whenever "The

00:03:40.310 --> 00:03:42.886
Last of Us" Season 2 finally commences filming.

